       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Carbamazepine:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " test for HLA-B*1502 before starting in patients with ancestry in populations where it may be present; don't use it in HLA-B*1502-positive patients unless the benefits clearly outweigh the risks (SJS/TEN)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Carbamazepine boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " aplastic anemia and agranulocytosis (risk 5 to 8 times that of the general population); get complete pretreatment hematologic testing as a baseline, monitor closely if WBC or platelet counts fall, and consider stopping for significant bone marrow depression."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Lamotrigine boxed warning (serious skin rashes): risk may rise with valproate, exceeding the recommended initial dose or dose escalation, or the HLA-B*1502 allele; cases have occurred without these factors."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Topiramate can cause hyperchloremic, non-anion gap metabolic acidosis (renal bicarbonate loss from carbonic anhydrase inhibition); measure serum bicarbonate at baseline and periodically, and if acidosis persists consider reducing the dose or stopping (with a taper)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Acute myopia with secondary angle-closure glaucoma: can cause permanent visual loss; stop topiramate as soon as possible. Metabolic acidosis: baseline and periodic serum bicarbonate recommended."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
